
Day 62 /100 of #DrGViswanathanChallenge

Today, I solved LeetCode 105 – Construct Binary Tree from Preorder and Inorder Traversal.

- Approach:
I used recursion + HashMap to efficiently construct the binary tree.
In preorder, the first element is always the root.
Use a HashMap to store the index of every value in the inorder traversal.
Find the root's position in inorder to divide the tree into:
Left subtree: elements before the root
Right subtree: elements after the root
Recursively construct both subtrees.
Maintain an index in preorder to process each root exactly once.

-Time Complexity : O(N) 
-Space Complexity : O(N) 

-Key Takeaways:
1) Preorder helps identify the root
2)  Inorder helps divide the tree into left and right subtrees
3) HashMap makes finding the root position efficient
4) Recursion makes the tree construction clean and intuitive
5) Strengthened my understanding of tree traversal relationships

